  "groundingSupports": [
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 119,
        "endIndex": 431,
        "text": "### **Candidate [1]: Anthropic’s best AI model struggles to attract corporate users**\n* **Confirmed:** A *Financial Times* report published on 23 August 2026 reveals that enterprise spending on Anthropic’s flagship model, Fable 5, has plateaued at approximately 11% of total customer spend on Anthropic tools"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 433,
        "endIndex": 539,
        "text": "The finding is based on spending data across 70,000 companies collected by corporate payment provider Ramp"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 541,
        "endIndex": 741,
        "text": "The report also notes Anthropic’s annualized revenue reached $65 billion in July (up from $47 billion in May), while OpenAI’s annualized revenue reached $40 billion following the launch of GPT 5.6"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 743,
        "endIndex": 866,
        "text": "* **Caveats:** Ramp data represents a specific subset of corporate credit card spend, not total global enterprise contracts"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 868,
        "endIndex": 960,
        "text": "Fable 5 experienced short-term availability disruptions in June following regulatory reviews"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1106,
        "endIndex": 1411,
        "text": "### **Candidate [2]: US corporate capex surge vs Europe driven by AI (Oxford Economics / FT)**\n* **Confirmed:** According to an Oxford Economics report covered by the *Financial Times* on 24 August 2026, real US corporate spending on equipment and facilities is projected to rise 40% between 2021 and 2027"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
